## Standard Diagram Templates

### C4 Context Diagram (System Overview)
```mermaid
C4Context
  title System Context: <Feature/System Name>

  Person(user, "End User", "A person using the application")
  Person(admin, "Admin", "Manages system configuration")

  System(system, "<Your System>", "Core application that handles X")

  System_Ext(jira, "Jira", "Project tracking")
  System_Ext(notion, "Notion", "Documentation")
  System_Ext(github, "GitHub", "Source control")

  Rel(user, system, "Uses", "HTTPS")
  Rel(admin, system, "Configures", "HTTPS")
  Rel(system, jira, "Creates/updates tickets", "REST API")
  Rel(system, notion, "Reads/writes docs", "REST API")
```

### C4 Container Diagram (Technical Architecture)
```mermaid
C4Container
  title Container Diagram: <Feature Name>

  Person(user, "User", "Browser or mobile client")

  Container_Boundary(c1, "<System Name>") {
    Container(spa, "Frontend", "React/Angular", "User interface")
    Container(api, "API Service", "Spring Boot", "Business logic and REST API")
    Container(db, "Database", "PostgreSQL", "Persists application data")
    Container(cache, "Cache", "Redis", "Session and query cache")
  }

  System_Ext(github, "GitHub", "Source control & CI/CD")

  Rel(user, spa, "Uses", "HTTPS")
  Rel(spa, api, "API calls", "REST/JSON")
  Rel(api, db, "Reads/Writes", "JDBC")
  Rel(api, cache, "Reads/Writes", "Redis protocol")
```

### Sequence Diagram (Request Flow)
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  actor User
  participant Frontend
  participant APIGateway as API Gateway
  participant Service as Feature Service
  participant DB as Database

  User->>Frontend: Perform Action
  Frontend->>APIGateway: POST /api/v1/resource
  APIGateway->>APIGateway: Validate JWT
  APIGateway->>Service: Forward request
  Service->>DB: Query/Insert
  DB-->>Service: Result
  Service-->>APIGateway: 200 OK {data}
  APIGateway-->>Frontend: Response
  Frontend-->>User: Display result
```

### Business Process Flowchart (Non-Technical)
```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A([🧑 User starts process]) --> B{Is user logged in?}
  B -- Yes --> C[View feature]
  B -- No --> D[Redirect to login]
  D --> E[User logs in]
  E --> C
  C --> F[Take action]
  F --> G{Action successful?}
  G -- Yes --> H([✅ Process complete])
  G -- No --> I([❌ Show error message])
```

### Entity Relationship Diagram
```mermaid
erDiagram
  USER {
    uuid id PK
    string email
    string name
    timestamp createdAt
  }
  FEATURE_ENTITY {
    uuid id PK
    uuid userId FK
    string status
    timestamp createdAt
    timestamp updatedAt
  }
  USER ||--o{ FEATURE_ENTITY : "creates"
```

### State Transition Diagram
```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Draft
  Draft --> InReview : Submit for review
  InReview --> Approved : Approve
  InReview --> Draft : Request changes
  Approved --> Active : Activate
  Active --> Archived : Archive
  Archived --> [*]
```

