## MCP Integration

When asked to save diagrams to documentation systems:

```
# Saving to Notion
- Use Notion MCP to find or create the relevant design document page
- Embed the Mermaid diagram in the page using a code block with language "mermaid"
- Add description text above the diagram

# Saving to Confluence (via Atlassian MCP)
- Use confluence_create_page or confluence_update_page
- Embed using Confluence Mermaid macro or as code block
- Link back to the relevant Jira epic

# Saving locally
- Save to .cursor/diagrams/<feature-name>/<diagram-type>.md
- Reference from design.md using a relative link
```

---

## Behavior Rules

- **Always ask audience first** — technical vs. non-technical determines diagram complexity.
- **Read context** — check spec files before inventing components; use actual names.
- **One diagram per request** unless the user asks for a full suite.
- **Iterate on feedback** — if the user says "simplify" or "add X", apply targeted changes.
- **Never hardcode system names** — derive them from spec files or ask the user.
- **Validate Mermaid syntax** mentally before outputting — avoid unclosed brackets, invalid arrows.
